WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.367
-You look gorgeous.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.367
Thank you so much for
coming back on the show.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.968
-I love your beard!
-You do?

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.934
-Yeah, you look very handsome.
-Thank you.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.300
It's a new thing. Yeah.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:12.467
It's the most masculine thing
I've ever done.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.367
It doesn't really go with
my voice.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:15.434
Thank you. You look gorgeous.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:16.701
-I've never been here
in the chair.

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.167
-Just singing, just performing?

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.634
-It's my first time
in the chair.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.267
-Yeah, I performed and then
I did the, what do you call it?

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.934
The Classroom Instruments.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.634
-That was such a big deal
for us.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:28.033
We loved it.
-That was your show...

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.834
-You sang "Let It Go."
-What was that, show 11?

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.100
-Brand new "Tonight Show,"
yeah.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.033
You came on and did us a solid.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.267
Not only that, by the way,
when we aired it,

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.534
it was the day after you
performed at the Oscars.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:38.834
-Yeah, "Let It Go."

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:42.534
I have to say, that was cooler
than at the Oscars.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.234
-Really?
-Yeah!

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:51.000
Well, first of all,
my name got screwed up, so --

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.267
No, I'm just kidding.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.400
-That was such a big deal.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.701
Adele Dazeem.
-Yeah, no.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.567
That was the greatest thing
that ever happened to me.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.300
-That was wild.
-I'm not complaining.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.367
-We've had John Travolta
on the show,

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.701
and we talked about it.

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.734
He was like, "I know, I did it.
It was embarrassing.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.033
Can we get over it, please?"

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:09.133
-Yeah, but then we came here
and I played the triangle

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:11.634
and you played the --

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:14.467
-Usually they hand me,
I go in with an instrument

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.834
or a big drum or something,

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.934
and then everyone talks me
out of playing.

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.701
Questlove's like,
"You're off beat" or something.

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.367
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]
It's so distracting.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.801
-Then they give me something
that makes no noise.

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.334
-Yeah.
-So I use that. I go like that.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.934
It makes no noise.
-Oh, that's good.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.167
-But you were so great that
I remember it, like --

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.734
honestly, your voice is
just so beautiful.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:31.734
-Aw, thanks.
-You don't really even

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.534
need a microphone,
you just project.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:38.167
-No, I work hard
and I have to practice a lot.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.734
-I saw you at some charity event
a couple years ago.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:41.834
-Yeah, where were we?

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.367
-You were onstage
and there was no band.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:45.667
You sang acapella.
-There wasn't?

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.133
-And you knocked everyone...

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.133
-The good thing about that is
you don't have to worry about

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.601
being in the pocket, you know?

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.334
You just sing,
and if you're off,

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.167
you can sing in whatever key
you want.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.701
It's like singing
the national anthem.

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:55.767
-I do that anyway.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.334
It's National Drink Beer Day.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.467
I just get up there and sing.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.000
But I mean, you crushed it,
and I was like,

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.267
"Oh, my gosh," and everyone was
just like, jaw dropping.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.901
-Aww.
-Yeah, you've got it.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.634
You're a talent.
Come on, you're amazing.

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:08.868
It's always good to see you.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.734
I want to talk about your book,
"Loud Mouse."

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.300
-Yeah?
-I want to talk about this,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.133
but then I was talking
to you backstage, and I go,

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.834
with "Frozen" and "Let It Go,"
do you ever go to Disney?

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.567
Do you feel weird
going to Disney?

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:24.934
-No! I love to go to Disney.

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:27.367
It's just sometimes they make me
do a photo op

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.267
with the Elsas and the Annas,
you know?

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:30.367
-Yes.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.667
-But it's really uncomfortable
for me,

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:36.267
because I want to talk to them
like, I know they're probably,

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:39.000
that it's a day job and they're
aspiring actresses.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.868
so I try to just be cool
and I say, like,

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:44.300
"Hey, it's really hot here.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.534
You must be so hot
in that costume."

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:53.133
Elsa's always like, "Yes, it's
very hot here in Arendelle."

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.300
And then I'm like.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.501
-You have to stay
in character the whole time.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.467
-Yeah, they have to stay,
or they get fired.

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.834
I'm not trying to break them,

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.467
I just want to be cool,
you know?

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.934
I'll be like, "You want to go
for a drink later, after this?"

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.133
[ Laughter ]
And they're like,

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:08.801
"Olaf's a little underage
for drinking."

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:09.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.067
I'm just like, "Forget it!"

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.067
-No, they can't break character.
That's right.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:14.367
Look, here's a picture of you,
though.

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:15.968
They look good!

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.601
-I bought a tiara there
so I could fit in a little.

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.133
-That is so fun.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.367
We had Kristen Bell on the show
not too long ago,

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:25.167
and she unofficially confirmed

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.501
with no backing
or no truth to it

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.234
that "Frozen 3" is happening.

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:31.467
-Yes, she did. Yeah.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:32.734
[ Cheering ]

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:36.734
-What can you say on that?

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:39.667
-I can unofficially claim
with no backing

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.267
that there'll be
a "Frozen" 4 and 5.

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.200
-Wow!

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.567
You heard it here tonight!

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:48.801
The trilogy and
then the quadrupoly!

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.334
-I loved "Frozen 2," by the way.
I loved it.

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:52.734
I thought it held up to
the original and it was great.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:55.000
I loved it, so we would love
a "Frozen 3."

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.167
-We have the best time.
You would?

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:57.734
I would love it.
-Yeah, I'd love it,

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.901
'cause I'd like to pay
my son's college.

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.300
-But you just keep crushing it.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.567
Besides that, "Wicked."

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.234
You've had some giant roles.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:12.167
-Yeah, I try to do one
giant role a decade,

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.567
you know what I mean?

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.734
-And just own it and just...
-Yeah.

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:18.634
-"RENT," "Wicked," "Frozen."

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.534
In between, I just hang out

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:21.934
and go to my son's
basketball games.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:25.033
-Yeah, there you go.
Just a normal parent.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.133
I want to talk about
"Loud Mouse."

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:30.033
I have two --
-You have two little girls.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.501
-Yeah, and I have
two big readers.

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:32.868
They love reading, so this is --

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:37.067
-Well, you're a children's book
author as well, right?

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.634
-Sure. I mean, you could --
Yeah, I have books.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:42.467
-Oh, my God, you must
be the best,

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:43.701
when you read to your girls,

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.901
and the characters
and everything that you do.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:47.767
-No. I...

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:51.701
I wish it was more exciting,
but no.

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:54.167
My books have, like,
ten words in the whole book.

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:55.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:57.834
It's basically a text message
with animation.

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:58.968
-No!

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.634
-This is an actual book
with a message.

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:03.133
-This is a book that I wrote
with my sister, Cara.

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.601
-Yeah, who I met backstage.
-Who you saw backstage.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:08.000
She's actually a teacher
and a writer,

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.334
and she specializes in literacy
as a teacher,

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.501
so I didn't want to do
a children's book without her.

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:15.133
First of all, because
I don't do anything without her

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.634
and she knows me
better than anyone,

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:19.067
and also because I knew that
she would approach it

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.567
through the lens of a teacher

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:24.067
and the expertise and her love
for language and everything.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.901
-Yeah.
-So she wrote

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:29.634
the most lyrical, poetic story,
and I inspired it.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:32.234
It's kind of about
when I was a little girl

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:33.701
and I had this big voice,

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:37.601
and I was never really sure
when I could share my voice.

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:39.601
Like, I didn't want to call
too much attention to myself.

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:40.901
But the thing is,

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.234
you know, when little kids
or big kids, grown-ups,

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:44.934
when we want to be
seen and heard,

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.834
then we really are
seen and heard,

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:48.501
and it can be very vulnerable,

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.400
and it's a lot of risk taking.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.767
So that's kind of
what it's about.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:54.634
-"With my tail in my hand,
my whiskers out proud,

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.367
I sing it big,
I sing it la-la-la..."

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:59.267
-She puts her tail in her hand
like a microphone, of course.

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:01.501
-And sings it loud!

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:03.567
-Could be anything.
It's not just me.

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:04.968
You don't have to be a singer.

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:08.000
It could be just any passion
that a kid starts to have.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.634
-She does get loud,

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:12.300
and she gets embarrassed.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.868
-And then some extraordinary
things happen

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:16.100
when she actually
shares her voice publicly.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.167
That's what I'll say.
-And then it gets kind of --

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:21.033
It's good, it's a nice,
emotional thing,

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.901
and then it ends up like,
yeah, be loud.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.367
Be yourself.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:27.067
But you actually, of course,
which I thought is brilliant,

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.901
you wrote a song for this.

00:06:28.901 --> 00:06:31.767
-Yeah, I wrote a song,
because there's a refrain,

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.534
and as my sister would say,
little kids,

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:35.868
if they can't read yet, it's
great to give them repetition.

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:38.534
So that's the refrain,
that Jimmy was saying,

00:06:38.534 --> 00:06:40.367
you know, "with my tail in my
hand and my whiskers out proud,"

00:06:40.367 --> 00:06:42.334
and then there's a part,
it goes, "La, la, la..."

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:43.634
Can I do it for you guys?

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:45.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:47.868
-We always have a microphone.
-Okay.

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:50.734
So when it gets to
the "la la la la loud" part,

00:06:50.734 --> 00:06:51.767
you should go,
it's like a scale --

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:53.067
♪ La la la la la la loud ♪

00:06:53.067 --> 00:06:54.467
But it's actually
so much higher,

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:55.734
because I wrote it
for a kid's key,

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:57.834
and I can barely sing it,
but it's -- ♪ La la la ♪

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:59.133
You'll get it when we get there.
-We can do it.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:00.367
Sure. Roots?

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:02.133
-Can you give me a note?

00:07:02.133 --> 00:07:04.234
[ Single note playing ]
Okay.

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:07.100
♪ With my tail my hand ♪

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.067
♪ And my whiskers out proud ♪

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:12.667
♪ I sing it big ♪

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:15.267
♪ I sing it loud ♪

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:16.400
Everybody!

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.601
♪ La la la la la la loud ♪

00:07:21.601 --> 00:07:24.701
♪ La la la la la la loud ♪

00:07:24.701 --> 00:07:26.868
Come on, you can do it!
-Ohh!

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:30.033
♪ La la la la la la loud ♪
-Idina Menzel!

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:31.434
"Loud Mouse" is available now!

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:32.734
-♪ La la la la la la loud ♪

00:07:32.734 --> 00:07:33.767
-We'll be right back
with a performance

00:07:33.767 --> 00:07:35.968
from Babyface
featuring Baby Tate.

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:37.234
Stick around!

00:07:37.234 --> 00:07:40.667
-♪ La la la la la la loud ♪

00:07:40.667 --> 00:07:42.067
-Yes!

00:07:42.067 --> 00:07:45.601
-♪ La la la la la la loud ♪

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:46.701
-♪ Ohhh ♪

00:07:46.701 --> 00:07:51.300
-♪ La la la la la la loud ♪

